course: dictionary
lesson: 12865
title: Enlargement: bigger, but the same shape
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An enlargement is the act of making something bigger. You can spot the word by its parts: en-large-ment, where large means big. «The shop made an enlargement of my holiday photo.» The photo is now bigger, but the people and the beach look just the same.
explain: In maths, an enlargement changes the size of a shape but keeps its shape. «Triangle A has sides of 3 cm. After enlargement by a scale factor of 2, its sides are 6 cm.» Every length is multiplied by the same number, so the triangle is bigger and still the same shape.
explain: Enlargement can also make things smaller. A scale factor less than 1 shrinks a shape, so «the enlargement of the map» can mean a smaller copy. Always check the scale factor: if it is bigger than 1, the shape grows.
fact: Enlargement means the act of making something bigger.
fact: An enlargement is also a photo that has been printed or made bigger.
fact: In maths, an enlargement keeps the shape the same and changes only the size.
fact: A scale factor of 2 doubles every side, and the area becomes 4 times bigger.
fact: A scale factor less than 1 makes a shape smaller, so the word can mean shrinking too.
exercise: «The shop made an enlargement of my holiday photo, so it is much bigger now.» What does enlargement mean here? | A smaller, blurry photo | A photo taken in the dark | *A bigger copy of a photo | A new kind of camera
exercise: A shape is enlarged by a scale factor of 2. What happens to each side? | Each side is 2 cm longer | Each side stays the same length | *Each side is twice as long | Each side is half as long
exercise: «The builders finished the enlargement of the kitchen.» Which word shows that the kitchen was made bigger? | *enlargement | builders | kitchen | finished
test: A square has sides of 2 cm. After an enlargement with scale factor 3, how long is each side? | *6 cm | 5 cm | 8 cm | 9 cm
test: A square with sides of 2 cm is enlarged by a scale factor of 2. How many times bigger is its area? | 8 times | *4 times | 2 times | 3 times
exam: The scan showed an enlargement of the heart, so the doctor checked it again. What does enlargement mean here? | A photo of the heart taken in the dark | *A part of the body that has grown larger than normal | A part of the body that is missing | A new kind of medicine
